## 2. Surface Tint System

V2 uses **per-card solid tints** via `color-mix()` with brand tokens (no `linear-gradient` on product HTML). Copy the values from `NewUnera/dashboard-enhanced.html` `:root` when adding pages.

```css
/* Body — clean white canvas */
background: var(--brand-white);   /* NOT a grey wash */

/* Card surfaces — single color-mix each (canonical product pages) */
--surface-impact:   color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 22%, var(--brand-white));
--surface-action:   color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 14%, var(--brand-white));
--surface-cad-hub:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-light-blue) 12%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 32%, var(--brand-white)));
--surface-warm:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-earth) 12%, var(--brand-white));
--surface-sky:      color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 18%, var(--brand-white));
--surface-deep:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-deep-blue) 4%, var(--brand-white));
```

**Rule**: Never use a raw grey hex for card backgrounds. Always use a `--surface-*` token or a new `color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-*), var(--brand-white))`.

