## 7. Transactional / flow pages (Get UNERA CAD, Redeem UNERA CAD)

These patterns are implemented in `NewUnera/get-unera-cad.html` and `NewUnera/redeem-unera-cad.html`. **Copy the `:root` flow tokens** into any similar multi-step or quote-driven page.

### 7.1 Flow-only surface tokens (`:root`)

Add **after** the standard `--surface-*` block from §2:

```css
/* Flow surfaces — action vs neutral hierarchy (selection, prereqs, soft alerts) */
--surface-scatter:             color-mix(in srgb, var(--neutral-200) 38%, var(--brand-white));
--surface-action-green:        color-mix(in srgb, var(--fin-up) 6%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 36%, var(--brand-white)));
--surface-action-green-strong: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fin-up) 10%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 30%, var(--brand-white)));
--surface-warning-soft:        color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-yellow) 50%, white);
--surface-error-soft:          color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-red) 10%, white);
```

| Token | Role |
|-----|-----|
| `--surface-scatter` | Secondary panels: muted neutral tint (`neutral-200` → white). Trust copy, fee callouts, saved-method containers — **calm**, not “selected”. |
| `--surface-action-green` | **Hover / light selected** — cloud-blue into a whisper of `--fin-up` (8%). Signals “this is a positive path” without looking like raw money green. |
| `--surface-action-green-strong` | **Strong selected / completed prereq** — more `--fin-up` (14%). Pair with `border-color: var(--fin-up)` and text `--fin-up` where the UI marks completion. |
| `--surface-warning-soft` | Rate expiry, time-sensitive notices — `--brand-yellow` at 50% into white. Border: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--warning) 35%, transparent)`. |
| `--surface-error-soft` | Soft destructive or validation surfaces — `--brand-red` at 10% into white. **UI state**, not P&L (still §3). |

**Principles**

- **Positive selection** in flows uses **`--fin-up` + action-green surfaces**, not full-bleed deep-blue fills on large selection panels — reserve **deep blue** for **titles emphasis, stepper “current”, and processing “pulse”** only.
- **`--surface-scatter`** is the default “quiet” card background for redeem-style prereq grids; prerequisite cards on older get-flow stubs may still use `--neutral-100` — **prefer scatter + fin-up hover** for new work to match Redeem.

### 7.2 Primary CTA on flow pages

Primary buttons use **solid deep blue** (`--gradient-deep` is `var(--brand-deep-blue)` on product HTML):

```css
.btn-primary {
    background: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    color: var(--brand-white);
}
.btn-primary:hover:not(:disabled) {
    filter: brightness(0.92);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.3);
}
```

### 7.3 Stepper vs amounts (brand deep blue vs P&L `--fin-up` / `#1a7a5e`)

| Element | Token | Why |
|-----|-----|-----|
| Step circles **active / complete**, stepper progress bar | `var(--brand-deep-blue)` (via `--gradient-primary`) | Same as page titles — **brand** progression |
| Large amounts, “you receive”, charts, completed processing labels | `--fin-up` | **Financial** positive — **`#1a7a5e`** (§3), not brand light blue |

Do not paint step numbers in `--fin-up` unless the design explicitly ties the step to a numeric outcome.

### 7.4 Quote route micro-bar (distribution spirit)

Horizontal progress hint (e.g. route / liquidity):

```css
.track { background: var(--neutral-100); /* or neutral band */ }
.track-fill {
    background: var(--brand-deep-blue);
}
```

Solid fill — institutional route bar, not fin-up.

### 7.5 Processing tracker chips

| State | Background | Notes |
|-----|-----|-----|
| Pending | `--neutral-200`, muted icon | Waiting |
| Current | `var(--brand-deep-blue)`, white icon | In progress — **brand** pulse |
| Done | `--success` (`--fin-up`), white check | Completed — **financial** positive (`#1a7a5e`) |

### 7.6 Success hero icon (large check)

- Circle fill: **`var(--brand-deep-blue)`** (legacy: `--gradient-deep`)
- Outer rings: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--fin-up) 32%, transparent)` and `16%` for a soft **gain halo** (fin-up / `#1a7a5e` family)
- Optional badge (e.g. “fast”): **`--gradient-warm`** (yellow tint mix) with `--brand-deep-blue` glyph

### 7.7 Destination / rail review banners

When users must **recognize rail risk** at a glance:

- **Fiat / CAD (brand-aligned, cautious):** background `color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-red) 9%, var(--brand-white))`, border `rgba(171, 87, 112, 0.22)` — **caution** rail (mauve family; not the **fin-up** positive path)
- **Crypto / USDT (on-chain positive path):** e.g. `background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-light-blue) 12%, var(--brand-white))`, border `color-mix(in srgb, var(--fin-up) 22%, transparent)` — aligns with **--fin-up** for “delivery asset”

Pills: `.dest-pill.cad` → `--error` text on `rgba(171,87,112,0.12)`; `.dest-pill.usdt` → `--fin-up` on `--fin-up-bg`.

### 7.8 Focus rings on flow controls

- Default buttons: `outline: 3px solid rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.3)` (deep-blue tint) matches the primary CTA
- Secondary / inputs on white: `--brand-deep-blue` outline as elsewhere (§5, §9)

